 "summary": "The generalization of `norm_tateCurveAt_\u0394` to submultiplicative ultrametric normed commutative rings is sound: the two-sided bound via `norm_evalIntSeries_le_one` on `u` and its inverse `v` needs no multiplicative norm, and `NormedField.toNormedCommRing`/`NormedDivisionRing.to_normOneClass` mean the old field statement is subsumed. The new evaluation lemma and the rederived coefficient identities are faithful images of the formal `\u2124\u27e6X\u27e7` identities under the ring hom `evalIntSeries`, with nontrivial consumers in this PR.",
